While Nvidia has sought to reassure us all, there are several layers here, beginning with the unfortunate timing.
For example: 
  The company is systemically important for tech, markets and the economy;
  Investors tend to struggle to price in key-person and governance issues;

The so-called “key-man risk” looms large here, and it’s doubtful markets have adequately priced it in.
This will not be easy for the board to navigate.
